{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>May the words of my mouth be acceptable</b> — that the insolent not rule over him." "And the meaning of <b>my Rock</b> — lest he fear that the insolent will rule over him; and even if they were to rule over him, he has no redeemer from their hand besides Him. Therefore: \"YHWH my Rock and my redeemer.\""], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:27:54.876014374Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}